{"url": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/ioffice/22295/subview.do", "title": "Inbound Exchange", "text": "Inbound Exchange Jeonbuk National University Portal OASIS Main Page Login Office of International Affairs Main Page Login Admissions Announcements Undergraduate English Korean Chinese Graduate English Korean Chinese Dragon Project (Chinese Only) Chinese Korean GKS program About US Welcome to the OIA Staff Directory Global Partnerships Campus Location How to Reach JBNU Incoming Inbound Exchange The Feeling Korea Korean Language Course Outgoing Language Program Exchange Program Report FAQ Life at JBNU Visa Leave of Absence & Returning to School Insurance Scholarships Student Support New Student Adjustment Support Program Life Support Program Academic Support Program Career Support Program Notice Board Notice Sites 메뉴닫기 모바일 메뉴 열기 사이트맵 바로가기 Office of International Affairs Driving Innovation and Collaboration Across Borders as We Shape the Global Leaders of Tomorrow 홈으로 즐겨찾기 즐겨찾는 메뉴 닫기 메뉴추가하기 초기화 공유하기 닫기 페이스북 공유하기 트위터 공유하기 핀터레스트 공유하기 카카오스토리 공유하기 주소 공유하기 인쇄하기 Inbound Exchange /WEB-INF/jsp/k2web/com/cop/site/layout.jsp ioffice_JW_MS_K2WT001_S ■ Summary of Program 1. Introduction - Exchange program is for students from overseas sister universities who can acquire Korean language and culture and earn credits in their majors and other subjects. 2. Period of Study - 6 months(one semester) or 1 year(two semesters) 3. Academics - Undergraduate Studies / Graduate Studies(except AUEA) 4. Classes Description Undergraduate Graduate Available Subjects Major, Other Majors, Liberal Arts, Korean Courses for Foreign Students Major, Other Majors Available Credits Minimum 6 ~ Maximum 18 Minimum 3 ~ Maximum 9 ※ Graduate students can take fee-paying Korean Special Course. ■ Calendar (2021) Description 1st(Spring) Semester 2nd(Fall) Semester Nomination and Application Deadline December 31 June 30 Online Application December 31 June 30 Documents Screening November ~ January 5 May ~ July 5 Delivery of Admission Document (Certificate of Admission and Registration Information) December ~ January 10 June ~ July 10 Payment of Dormitory Fee January 20 ~ February 10 July 20 ~ August 10 Arrival in Korea February 27 ~ March 1 August 30 ~ August 31 Incheon Airport Pick-up Service February 27 August 30 Orientation February 28 August 31 Beginning of Semester March 2 September 1 Course Registration March 2 ~ March 6 September 1 ~ September 5 End of Semester June 20 December 24 ※ The date may change slightly every semester. ■ Online Application 1. Website : https://all.jbnu.ac.kr/jbnu/oasis/online_application.html 2. Application Period : ~ December 31, ~ June 30 ■ Required Documents 1. Application Form 2. Study Plan and Self-introduction in Korean or English 3. Academic Transcript 4. Certificate of Enrollment in English (If it is written in another language, required Korean translation.) 5. Letter of Recommendation in English (If it is written in another language, required Korean translation.) 6. Photocopy of Passport 7. 3 Photos(White background) 8. Tuberculosis Test Report(Chest X-Ray Examination) ■ Courses ※ Exchange students(undergraduate) can apply for at least 6 credits and up to 18 credits per semester. ※ Exchange students(Graduate) can apply for at least 3 credits and up to 9 credits per semester. ※ Exchange students can register for all classes of other grades. 1. Korean Courses for Foreign Students - Only for Undergraduate Exchange Students - Fee-free - Credit granting (3 courses = 9 credits) - Depending on the Korean language proficiency of exchange students, JBNU basically provides 3 courses in Korean language courses. 2. Korean Special Course for Graduate Students - Fee-paying, 450,000 KRW/semester(14 weeks, 70 hours), 13:00~14:00(Monday~Friday) Levels Subjects Credits Basic 1, 2 Speaking and Listening 3 Reading 3 Writing 3 Intermediate 1, 2 Speaking and Listening 3 Reading 3 Writing 3 Advanced 1, 2 Advanced Korean of Current Affairs 3 Advanced Korean of Video 3 Advanced Writing 3 - No credit - Conversation Class - 1 hour/day, 14 weeks, 13:00~14:00 - Levels : Basic / Intermediate / Advanced 3. Courses Taught in English(Credit granting courses) - School of International Studies Grade Semester Subject Credit-Lecture 1 1 Academic Reading and Writing Academic Debate and Presentation 3-3 3-3 2 Introduction to International Studies Introduction to International Development Reading Contemporary Korea 3-3 3-3 2 1 Introduction to Economics Social Research Design 3-3 3-3 Understanding International Law Area Studies 1 International Political Economy Introduction to Human Rights 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 Theories of International Relations Economic Development 3-3 3-3 Global Issues in Development Area Studies 2 International Organizations and Global Governance Quantitative Research Method 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3 1 Development Management ODA Policies in Global Development Strategy Culture and International Relations International Development Cooperation in Northeast Asia Area Studies 3 International Communication 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 Introduction to Public Diplomacy : Issues and Topics Politics of the Developing World International Ethics and Social Justice Public Diplomacy and Korea Qualitative Research Method 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 4 1 Advanced Topics in Human Rights and Security Gender, Politics and the Law Special Topics in Global Affairs : International Development Advanced Seminar on the Global South 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 International Negotiation Migration and Multiculturalism Advanced Seminar on the Korean Peninsula International Peace and Security 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 - School of International Engineering and Science Grade Semester Subject Credit-Lecture 2 1 Organic Chemistry Differential Equation Circuit Theory 1 Engineering Science C Language Discrete Structure Microbiology 1 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 Python Programming Data Structure Linear Algebra Organic Chemistry 2 Circuit Theory 2 Microbiology 2 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3 1 Basic Machine Learning Instruction to Algorism Polymer Science & Technique Digital Engineering 1 Probability and Statistics Genetics 1 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 Physical Chemistry Engineering of Semiconductor Digital Engineering 2 Creative Engineering Design 1 Fundamental of Bio-informatics Genetics 2 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 4 1 Creative Engineering Design 2 Mechatronics Display Engineering Biochemistry 1 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 2 Flexible and Printable Electronics Device for Energy Conversion Deep Learning Project Artificial Intelligence Robotics) Biochemistry 2 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 3-3 ※ In addition, students can choose major courses in English from each department. (Major courses in English vary on each semester. 4. Short-term Semester Session Period Course Registration Summer end of June ~ middle of July beginning of May Winter end of December ~ middle of January beginning of November - Credits : Students can apply for up to 6 credits. - Fee : 23,000 KRW/1credit 5. Official Transcript and Certificate of Completion - 1 st Semester : July 15 - 2 nd Semester : January 15 ※ The transcripts and certificates of completion will be sent by airmail to home universities of exchange students. ※ The transcript can be issued by the exchange student himself/herself through the certificate issuing machine installed on the first floor of the law school(4-1 Building). ■ Dormitory 1. Location: Chambit Building, Jeonbuk National University Residence Hall No.93 Changpo-gil, Deokjin-gu, Jeonju-si, Jeonbuk 54896 2. Payment of Dormitory Fee - Period : January 20 ~ February 10, July 20 ~ August 10 - Amount : Approximately 1,100,000 KRW 3. Others - Twin room - Serving 3 meals a day except Saturdays and Sundays - Each room is furnished with a desk, chair, wardrobe, bed, shoe rack, bookshelf, Internet, bathroom, shower room, phone, desk lamp, etc. ※ Dormitory does not provide bedding, so exchange students should prepare their own bedding and pillows. - Common Facilities : reading room, computer room, fitness room, laundry room(coin operated) - Amenities : convenience store, stationery store, cafe, restaurant, pizza/chicken place - Caution : light fire, smoking, drinking, and cooking are prohibited in dormitory, and students who violate the rules will leave immediately from dormitory by force. - Homepage : http://likehome.jbnu.ac.kr/ - Phone : 063-270-4723 ■ Insurance 1. Amount - Insurance Company : 110,000 KRW/year, 60,000 KRW/semester (Present) - National Health Insurance : 40,000 KRW/month or more (within the next few years) 2. Guarantee items : General hospital treatment cost, Medicine cost, Operation cost, Hospitalization cost, etc. (Cosmetic surgery, Dermatology and Dentistry cannot be reimbursed) - Regardless of the domestic insurance of home country, exchange students must join the insurance in Korea after entry. - Accidents caused by driving and riding motorcycles are not guaranteed. ■ Contacts - E-mail : inbound@jbnu.ac.kr, inboundct@jbnu.ac.kr(China, Taiwan), yunhap91@jbnu.ac.kr(AUEA-Southeast Asia) - Phone : 82-63-270-4757, 82-63-270-2184(China, Taiwan), 82-63-270-4892(AUEA-Southeast Asia) Privacy Policy Rejection of Unauthorized Email Collection 페이스북 바로가기 인스타그램 바로가기 유투브 바로가기 Address 567 BAEKJE-DAERO, DEOKJIN-GU, JEONJU-SI, JEONBUK STATE 54896 REPUBLIC OF KOREA Tel +82-63-270-2098 FAX +82-63-270-2099 Copyright (c) Jeonbuk National University. All rights reserved. Sites JEONBUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TOP"}
{"url": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/ioffice/22297/subview.do", "title": "The Feeling Korea", "text": "The Feeling Korea Jeonbuk National University Portal OASIS Main Page Login Office of International Affairs Main Page Login Admissions Announcements Undergraduate English Korean Chinese Graduate English Korean Chinese Dragon Project (Chinese Only) Chinese Korean GKS program About US Welcome to the OIA Staff Directory Global Partnerships Campus Location How to Reach JBNU Incoming Inbound Exchange The Feeling Korea Korean Language Course Outgoing Language Program Exchange Program Report FAQ Life at JBNU Visa Leave of Absence & Returning to School Insurance Scholarships Student Support New Student Adjustment Support Program Life Support Program Academic Support Program Career Support Program Notice Board Notice Sites 메뉴닫기 모바일 메뉴 열기 사이트맵 바로가기 Office of International Affairs Driving Innovation and Collaboration Across Borders as We Shape the Global Leaders of Tomorrow 홈으로 즐겨찾기 즐겨찾는 메뉴 닫기 메뉴추가하기 초기화 공유하기 닫기 페이스북 공유하기 트위터 공유하기 핀터레스트 공유하기 카카오스토리 공유하기 주소 공유하기 인쇄하기 The Feeling Korea /WEB-INF/jsp/k2web/com/cop/site/layout.jsp ioffice_JW_MS_K2WT001_S ■ Introduction This program not only provides an excellent education in the Korean language taught by excellent teachers but also takes full advantage of the excellent variety of local Korean cultural opportunities and experiences, such as Taekwondo and, traditional music. This is accomplished through interactions between students and volunteers who are responsible for interpreting and guiding foreign participants in order to increase mutual understanding of two cultures, making it possible to create a global mindset. Participants can experience the essence of both traditional and modern Korea as well various Korean cultural activities in a short period of time. ■ Period of the Program The program is held 1-2 times during each Summer / Winter vacation for two weeks. - Period: 2 weeks - Schedule · Morning: Korean Language Class for Foreigners · Afternoon: Korean Traditional Cultural Activities ■ Subject and Credits - Subject: Introduction to Korean Culture - Credits: 3(45hours) for 2 weeks ■ Participation Fee Contents Non-Sister Universities Sister Universities Mandatory Fees Including: Accommodation, Meals, Tuition, Field Trip, Transportation 1,000 USD 800 USD ■ Dormitory - Clean, comfortable dormitory - 2 People/Room - 3 meals a day (Weekend not included) - Each room is furnished with a desk, bookshelf, chair, bed, wardrobe, shoe rack, bathroom and Internet - Attached Facilities : laundry room, dining hall, convenience store, etc. - Common Room : lounge, seminar room, reading room, computer room, training room, AV room ■ Customized Programs - JBNU can design custom programs scheduled throughout the year for your organization or university. - Program fees will vary depending on the program period, contents, number of participants, and your particular requests. ■ Conta ct : feelingkorea@jbnu.ac.kr fnctId=pdfView,fnctNo=63 Feeling Korea Feeling Korea 다운로드(PDF) Privacy Policy Rejection of Unauthorized Email Collection 페이스북 바로가기 인스타그램 바로가기 유투브 바로가기 Address 567 BAEKJE-DAERO, DEOKJIN-GU, JEONJU-SI, JEONBUK STATE 54896 REPUBLIC OF KOREA Tel +82-63-270-2098 FAX +82-63-270-2099 Copyright (c) Jeonbuk National University. All rights reserved. Sites JEONBUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TOP"}
{"url": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/ioffice/22300/subview.do", "title": "Language Program", "text": "Language Program Jeonbuk National University Portal OASIS Main Page Login Office of International Affairs Main Page Login Admissions Announcements Undergraduate English Korean Chinese Graduate English Korean Chinese Dragon Project (Chinese Only) Chinese Korean GKS program About US Welcome to the OIA Staff Directory Global Partnerships Campus Location How to Reach JBNU Incoming Inbound Exchange The Feeling Korea Korean Language Course Outgoing Language Program Exchange Program Report FAQ Life at JBNU Visa Leave of Absence & Returning to School Insurance Scholarships Student Support New Student Adjustment Support Program Life Support Program Academic Support Program Career Support Program Notice Board Notice Sites 메뉴닫기 모바일 메뉴 열기 사이트맵 바로가기 Office of International Affairs Driving Innovation and Collaboration Across Borders as We Shape the Global Leaders of Tomorrow 홈으로 즐겨찾기 즐겨찾는 메뉴 닫기 메뉴추가하기 초기화 공유하기 닫기 페이스북 공유하기 트위터 공유하기 핀터레스트 공유하기 카카오스토리 공유하기 주소 공유하기 인쇄하기 Language Program /WEB-INF/jsp/k2web/com/cop/site/layout.jsp ioffice_JW_MS_K2WT001_S ■ 개요 - 목적: 어학실력 향상을 통한 글로벌 역량 강화 및 국제적 감각 향상 - 파견국가: 미국, 영국, 호주, 필리핀 등(매 학기 파견 국가는 변동 가능) - 파견일정: 1학기, 하계방학, 2학기, 동계방학 ■ 자격 1. 전북대학교 학부 재학생으로 파견 종료 후 8학기를 본교에서 수학 가능한자 ( 신 편입학 첫 학기 재학생, 졸업예정자, 졸업유예자, 해당학기 휴학생 지원 불가 ) 2. 학칙 위반 등으로 처벌된 경력이 없는 자 3. 국제협력부 어학연수 프로그램 동일 언어권 파견 경험이 없는 자 4. 외국인 유학생의 경우 TOPIK 4급 이상 보유자 ■ 지원방법 1. 지원기간 내 온라인 접수 후 원본 서류 제출 - 온라인접수 URL: http://all.jbnu.ac.kr/jbnu/oasis/index.html - 오아시스로그인-학사정보-국제교류-파견교환/어학연수학생용-파견교환/어학연수신청 2. 온라인 접수 후 지원서류 일체 국제협력부(뉴실크로드센터 3층) 직접 또는 우편 제출 ■ 제출서류 구분 순서 제출서류 필수 1 참가신청서 2 수학계획서 3 서약서 4 질병확인서 5 개인정보수집 및 이용동의서 6 재학증명서 7 전체학년 국문 성적증명서 8 본인명의 통장사본 선택 9 외국어능력시험 성적표 10 기초생활보장수급자 입증서류 ■ 문의처 : offcampus@jbnu.ac.kr Privacy Policy Rejection of Unauthorized Email Collection 페이스북 바로가기 인스타그램 바로가기 유투브 바로가기 Address 567 BAEKJE-DAERO, DEOKJIN-GU, JEONJU-SI, JEONBUK STATE 54896 REPUBLIC OF KOREA Tel +82-63-270-2098 FAX +82-63-270-2099 Copyright (c) Jeonbuk National University. All rights reserved. Sites JEONBUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TOP"}
{"url": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/ioffice/22301/subview.do", "title": "Exchange Program", "text": "Exchange Program Jeonbuk National University Portal OASIS Main Page Login Office of International Affairs Main Page Login Admissions Announcements Undergraduate English Korean Chinese Graduate English Korean Chinese Dragon Project (Chinese Only) Chinese Korean GKS program About US Welcome to the OIA Staff Directory Global Partnerships Campus Location How to Reach JBNU Incoming Inbound Exchange The Feeling Korea Korean Language Course Outgoing Language Program Exchange Program Report FAQ Life at JBNU Visa Leave of Absence & Returning to School Insurance Scholarships Student Support New Student Adjustment Support Program Life Support Program Academic Support Program Career Support Program Notice Board Notice Sites 메뉴닫기 모바일 메뉴 열기 사이트맵 바로가기 Office of International Affairs Driving Innovation and Collaboration Across Borders as We Shape the Global Leaders of Tomorrow 홈으로 즐겨찾기 즐겨찾는 메뉴 닫기 메뉴추가하기 초기화 공유하기 닫기 페이스북 공유하기 트위터 공유하기 핀터레스트 공유하기 카카오스토리 공유하기 주소 공유하기 인쇄하기 Exchange Program /WEB-INF/jsp/k2web/com/cop/site/layout.jsp ioffice_JW_MS_K2WT001_S ■ 해외파견 프로그램이란? 국제적 감각과 인문학적 소양을 갖춘 다재다능한 인재를 요구하고 있는 현대사회에 부응하기 위하여 재학기간 중 해외 자매대학으로 파견하여 전공 관련 정규 교육과정을 이수 후 학점을 취득하고, 해외문화 체험 등 다양한 활동을 통해 글로벌 능력을 배양 및 사고의 폭 확대를 통한 인재양성하는 프로그램 ■ 파견 국가 독일, 말레이시아 , 미국, 스페인, 영국, 일본, 중국, 폴란드 , 프랑스, 이탈리아 등 ■ 운영시기 - 파견시기 : 1년 2회(학기 별) - 선발시기 2~4월, 8~10월 ■ 장학혜택 (파견 기간과 관계없이 파견 시 1회 수혜 가능) - 1인당 100만원(아시아권) - 1인당 200만원(비아시아권) ■ 학점인정 - 학기 중 최소 6학점 ~ 최대 18학점 ■ 제출서류 구 분 순 제 출 서 류 필 수 1 참가신청서 (서식 1) 2 수학계획서 (국문서식 2, 파견국가 언어 서식 2-1) 3 파견교환학생 서약서 (서식 3) 4 질병확인서 (서식 4) 5 개인정보 수집·이용 동의서 (서식 5) 6 재학증명서 국문, 영문 각 1부 7 전체학년 성적증명서 국문, 영문 각 1부 (국문 성적증명서: 100점 만점 점수 표기 필수) 8 외국어능력시험 성적표 원본, 사본 각 1부 (원본 확인 후 반환) 9 여권 사본 1부 (여권유효잔여기간이 출국일 기준 12개월 이상 남아있을 것) * 여권 미소지자 또는 기간 만료자의 경우 : 여권발급 신청 후, 여권발급이 완료되는 즉시 여권사본 1부 추가 제출 10 본인명의 통장사본 1부 기 타 1 복학서약서 1부 (서식6, 휴학생에 한함) 2 기초생활보장수급자 입증서류 1부 (해당자에 한함) ■ 전형방법 및 선발기준 가. 전형방법 학부성적 : 100점 서류심사 및 면접심사 : 100점 가산점 : 기초생활보장수급자, 언어교육부 수업 수강자(최근2년) 1. 학부성적 : 직전학기 성적(백분율) 점수 적용 2. 수학계획서를 바탕으로 지원자의 역량 및 프로그램 취지에 맞는 학업계획 평가 ※ 각 항목별(학부성적 및 서류 및 면접) 점수 70점 미만인 자는 불합격 처리 **매 학기 선발마다 파견 국가, 언어조건 등 상이하므로 전북대학교 홈페이지(교내공지)를 통해 확인 ■ 문의메일 outbound@jbnu.ac.kr Privacy Policy Rejection of Unauthorized Email Collection 페이스북 바로가기 인스타그램 바로가기 유투브 바로가기 Address 567 BAEKJE-DAERO, DEOKJIN-GU, JEONJU-SI, JEONBUK STATE 54896 REPUBLIC OF KOREA Tel +82-63-270-2098 FAX +82-63-270-2099 Copyright (c) Jeonbuk National University. All rights reserved. Sites JEONBUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TOP"}
